course: dictionary
lesson: 11574
title: One word, many meanings: annex
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Annex is a word with more than one meaning, so you need the clues around it to know which one is right. «The school annexe has two new art rooms.» Here an annexe is an extra building joined to the main school.
explain: Annex can also be an action word. «The king wanted to annex the land next to his own.» The clues are king and land: here annex means to take control of land and make it part of your own country, usually by force and without agreement.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «to take land and make it part of my own country» fit? Then you have found the right meaning. If the sentence is about a report or a form, annex means an extra part added to it.
fact: An annex is an extra building joined to or near a main building.
fact: An annex can also be an extra part added to a document, such as a report or a form.
fact: To annex means to take control of land and make it part of your own country, usually by force and without agreement.
fact: To annex can also mean to add something as an extra part.
fact: Annexation is the noun for this act: most countries in the UN called Russia's annexation of Crimea illegal.
exercise: «The school annexe is across the playground.» What is an annexe here? | A big puddle after rain | *An extra building joined to the main school | A type of school bag | A tall tree in the playground
exercise: «The army wanted to annex the small country next door.» What does annex mean here? | *To take the land and make it part of their own country | To paint the walls of a house | To fold a letter neatly | To make a new friend at school
exercise: The report had an extra page added at the end. Find and copy the word that means an extra part added to a document. | playground | school | report | *annex
test: «Russia annexed Crimea.» Which word is the verb here? | the | Russia | Crimea | *annexed
test: Which sentence uses annex as a noun for a building? | «They annexed the village last year.» | «She will annex her notes to the letter.» | «The king will annex the valley.» | *«The annexe was built behind the library.»
exam: «The clerk added an annex to the report.» What does annex mean here? | *An extra part added to a document | A building for sports | A short walk in the park | To take control of a country by force
